  {
   "id": "L12e00244",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2900.0,
   "y": 2143.0,
   "width": 761.6,
   "height": 120.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "c03w",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 2032236,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 25753876,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Negro: as-is / legacy que sigue igual.   Rojo: SPOF y flujos alternos.\nAzul: nuevo con reliability / fault tolerance (New Architecture).\nNaranja: migracion evolutiva y piloto (router, ACL, feature flag, interceptor).\nVerde (grueso): critical path medicion -> decision -> refrigeracion / alarma.\nLinea solida = sincrono.   Punteada = asincrono (eventos, logs).\nCajas apiladas = instancias replicadas.  Recuadros: HOST / New Architecture / Legacy.",
   "originalText": "Negro: as-is / legacy que sigue igual.   Rojo: SPOF y flujos alternos.\nAzul: nuevo con reliability / fault tolerance (New Architecture).\nNaranja: migracion evolutiva y piloto (router, ACL, feature flag, interceptor).\nVerde (grueso): critical path medicion -> decision -> refrigeracion / alarma.\nLinea solida = sincrono.   Punteada = asincrono (eventos, logs).\nCajas apiladas = instancias replicadas.  Recuadros: HOST / New Architecture / Legacy.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "L12e00245",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2900.0,
   "y": 2330.0,
   "width": 593.6,
   "height": 25.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "c03x",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 2040155,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 25858605,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Criterios hipoteticos de escalabilidad (aun sin data)",
   "originalText": "Criterios hipoteticos de escalabilidad (aun sin data)",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "L12e00246",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2900.0,
   "y": 2363.0,
   "width": 743.6800000000001,
   "height": 320.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "c03y",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 2048074,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 25963334,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Load hipotetica: 300 sensores x 20 msg/s = 6 000 msg/s (518 M/dia).\nCUANDO escalar (dashboards: trafico, availability, reliability, latencia):\n - Latencia P99 medicion -> decision local: Good < 50 ms | OK < 100 | Bad > 100.\n - Latencia P99 Controller -> Main: Good < 200 ms | OK < 500 | Bad > 1 s.\n - Availability (2xx/(2xx+5xx)): Good >= 99.9% | OK >= 99.5% | Bad < 99.5%.\n - Trafico sostenido > 70% de la capacidad medida con load testing.\n Regla: trafico sube -> availability baja -> latencia sube => escalar.\n Pico transitorio (escenario 3) no se escala; caida subita (esc. 4) = RCA.\nQUE escalar: el bottleneck, hallado con perf testing (load/stress/spike/volume).\n Candidatos: ingesta del Main Controller, escrituras en Log DB, lecturas del panel.\nCOMO escalar (patron minimo necesario):\n - Computo -> scale out + LB (Main Controller stateless).\n - Datos -> Cache aside -> Read Replicas -> Sharding por reactor.\n - I/O escrituras -> Cola asincrona -> Write Replica.\n - Red -> Side-car en el mismo host.\n Nuevo reactor = nuevo shard (controller local propio).",
   "originalText": "Load hipotetica: 300 sensores x 20 msg/s = 6 000 msg/s (518 M/dia).\nCUANDO escalar (dashboards: trafico, availability, reliability, latencia):\n - Latencia P99 medicion -> decision local: Good < 50 ms | OK < 100 | Bad > 100.\n - Latencia P99 Controller -> Main: Good < 200 ms | OK < 500 | Bad > 1 s.\n - Availability (2xx/(2xx+5xx)): Good >= 99.9% | OK >= 99.5% | Bad < 99.5%.\n - Trafico sostenido > 70% de la capacidad medida con load testing.\n Regla: trafico sube -> availability baja -> latencia sube => escalar.\n Pico transitorio (escenario 3) no se escala; caida subita (esc. 4) = RCA.\nQUE escalar: el bottleneck, hallado con perf testing (load/stress/spike/volume).\n Candidatos: ingesta del Main Controller, escrituras en Log DB, lecturas del panel.\nCOMO escalar (patron minimo necesario):\n - Computo -> scale out + LB (Main Controller stateless).\n - Datos -> Cache aside -> Read Replicas -> Sharding por reactor.\n - I/O escrituras -> Cola asincrona -> Write Replica.\n - Red -> Side-car en el mismo host.\n Nuevo reactor = nuevo shard (controller local propio).",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
